{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RESIDUAL-GAP MATERIAL — LLM-Review advisories harvested from Gerrit (all non-blocking):\n 2503 (5): (1) _facade_function falls open -> FIXED IN SCOPE. (2) co_names parity not enforced, with\n   FIVE unflagged real mismatches in the shipped manifest -> FIXED IN SCOPE. (3) STALE DIVERGENCE\n   path untested. (4) merge_declarations carry-forward untested. (5) _check_normalization untested.\n 2505 (1): the adoption-half tests assert on source TEXT rather than behavior.\n 2506 (4): (1) the oracle redefines _load/_kinds/guard twice -> FIXED IN SCOPE (see below).\n   (2) _check_home_escape may over-flag any argv mentioning home/mkdtemp/TemporaryDirectory.\n   (3) the UsageError contract is verified only by grepping conftest text. (4) the file-level opt-out\n   fallback for helper-hosted hazards is untested.\n 2504: none.\n\nFIXED THE 2506 DUPLICATION — and the reviewer was right where I had been wrong. My earlier dedupe\nattempt reported 'duplicate block not found' and I moved on; the duplication was in fact present\n(_load, guard = _load(), and _kinds each defined twice). Ruff did not flag it, so the failed\nassertion was my only signal and I misread it as absence. Removed 15 lines; 27/27 still pass. The\nsecond definitions had been winning at runtime, so behavior was unaffected — it was dead duplication,\nnot a behavioral defect, but it was real.\nRequired a THIRD stacked amend of 2506 plus a rebase of the two commits above it. Final stack:\n 6ecba4218c86 2503 parity -> e456f39d625c 2504 mirrors -> 05f6963023dc 2505 atomic ->\n 94efaf5b0192 2506 guard -> 000c862c22c7 2507 measurement -> 9226c81d5545 (new) ratchet\n\nSELF-INFLICTED TEST ERROR WORTH RECORDING: my first full-tier run errored with 'The repo HEAD moved\nduring this test (94efaf5b01 -> 000c862c22)' — the repo-isolation guard correctly catching that I ran\nthe rebase WHILE the suite was executing. 1883 passed / 5 skipped / 1 error, and the error was purely\nthat concurrency artifact. Same one-writer-per-worktree lesson as the two-subagent case earlier,\nthis time me against my own test run. Re-running on a stable tree with no concurrent git operations."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788324585737946001,"uuid":"7314ff02-918c-4948-9aa5-4bded1299968"}